  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>From Gigaro beach, the coastal path enters the Domaine du Cap Lardier, a Conservatoire du littoral site where scrubland and coves offer views of Cap Taillat and the Îles d'Or. According to La Croix-Valmer Tourisme, the yellow-waymarked coastal path is 11 km return with 103 m of elevation gain (blue level, moderate, rock and earth, not suitable for pushchairs). It is open all year, weather permitting, with free access. At the end, La Briande beach is a 45-minute walk from Gigaro, with no other access.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs are accepted in the Domaine du Cap Lardier, on a leash only, as the coastal path is narrow (Port-Cros and Porquerolles National Park, tourist office). On beaches, they may only go onto them to cross. For beaches the tourist office gives a precise rule: dogs prohibited on all beaches 7am-8pm from 1 May to 30 October, allowed on a leash outside those hours and that period. The terrain is rocky and exposed: bring water, a hat and good shoes.</p>
      <p>The national park recalls the site rules (prefectoral order of 3 May 2023): camping and bivouac strictly prohibited, including on beaches and in the forest, any source of fire banned, stay on tracks and paths and do not cross fences. There are bins only at the site entrance: take your dog's waste with you. Gigaro parking is paid from 1 June to 30 September, 9am to 7pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: bring plenty of water, avoid the hottest hours and check your dog's paw pads at the end of the walk.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>La Croix-Valmer and its beaches are close by, and Cap Taillat offers one of the finest viewpoints on the Var coast.</p>
